LORE.push(
  {ch:413, n:'Two Women in His Head', t:'Levi admitted to Jade that Sally and the princess he spent years searching for occupy different places in his mind: a friend and colleague, and an unfinished mission. He would not merge them or approach Sally with a half-truth.'},
  {ch:414, n:'Nothing Has Changed', t:'At the usual evening drinks, Levi was quiet and careful. Sally noticed him choosing his words and was not convinced when he said nothing had changed.'},
  {ch:415, n:'The Friend Who Knows Too Much', t:'Carly noticed Sally had been quiet and tired. Sally admitted that Levi looked at her as someone real, and that this frightened her. Carly told her to be honest with herself and not to push him away out of fear.'},
  {ch:416, n:'The Royal Melody', t:'A royal chamber melody found by Adrian in the northern archives was played at Sally\'s tavern. Sally stopped the musicians and asked for the older, more refined arrangement. She knew it without hesitation, but royal music can be taught, so it proved nothing.'},
  {ch:417, n:'Do Not Look at Me Like That', t:'After closing, Sally asked Levi why he had been so careful and distant. He told her they were investigating the past and people she is connected to, and promised to tell her himself once he had proof. Sally hid the hurt; her feelings for him had only grown stronger.'},
  {ch:418, n:'The Truth They Suspect', t:'Jade told Sally that she may be the missing princess of Lysenne. Sally answered with anger and disbelief, refusing to have another identity placed on her. She asked for time and for the matter to stay private until there is proof.'},
  {ch:419, n:'Sally Sin', t:'Sally told Levi that whatever the investigation uncovers, the life she lived afterward is hers. She would not become a symbol, a political tool or a memory to be restored: I am Sally Sin, not a crown, not a kingdom, not a ghost from the past. Levi promised her choice would be respected.'},
  {ch:420, n:'The Tavern Beyond the Gates', t:'For one night Sally and Levi left the investigation behind at a quiet tavern outside Dragonvale\'s gates. They spoke more honestly than usual, admitted that things had changed and that they could not go back to pretending they were only allies, and agreed not to define anything that night.'},
  {ch:421, n:'Morning Without Promises', t:'The morning after, neither regretted the night. When Levi spoke of responsibility Sally stopped him: she would not be an obligation, a wife or a political arrangement. They agreed to keep it between them, with no titles and no promises, for now.'},
  {ch:422, n:'One Night Is One Night', t:'Back in her manor, Sally told Carly that nothing had changed: one night is one night. Carly saw through it. Sally realised that leaving had been easy; what was dangerous was how much she had wanted to stay.'},
  {ch:423, n:'A Princess\'s Nurse', t:'An elderly nurse who had cared for the missing princess remembered a bright, curious child with a hidden birthmark near the shoulder blade and a habit of tapping her fingers when anxious, but could not say which side the mark was on or what the pattern was. Jade said these were only clues, though Sally found the habit familiar.'},
  {ch:424, n:'The Girl Before Sally', t:'A former servant of Lysenne\'s royal household told Sally of a lively child who followed the older princess everywhere, and of how she was hidden and moved between safe houses under a different name. She gave Sally a keepsake that had belonged to the princess.'},
  {ch:425, n:'Levi Steps Back', t:'After the meeting with the nurse and the servant, Levi grew quiet and distant. Sally feared he regretted their night; he did not, he simply could not process everything at once. She chose not to chase him for answers.'},
  {ch:426, n:'Not Regret', t:'Levi told Sally plainly that he did not regret their night. He had once devoted himself to finding the princess, and Sally had become someone real to him independently; he needed time to understand what that meant. Sally promised him time and asked that he not disappear without a word.'},
  {ch:427, n:'More Than I Intended', t:'Sally admitted to Carly that Levi had become more than a passing attraction, and that this was exactly why she did not want to commit: she did not want to be the reason he abandoned everything else. Carly told her that stepping back is also a kind choice.'},
  {ch:430, n:'What Marriage Taught Her', t:'Alone in her Dragonvale manor, Sally reflected on her marriage: she had hoped for stability and respectability and found herself trapped. Lucien taught her that duty cannot become love by wearing love\'s name. She would not rush into another cage, even for Levi.'},
  {ch:432, n:'The Last Witness', t:'A last witness who had served Princess Zhaoning recognised Sally by a three-note finger rhythm and a birthmark near the right shoulder blade, which Jade verified in private. Zhaoning had survived and grown into Sally Sin. Her half-sister Zhaohua had survived too, for a time under the name Orchid.'}
);

