LORE.push(
  {ch:465, n:'No Court Robes Tomorrow', t:'The party took several days off in a coastal village. When an urgent message arrived from the capital Jade put it aside until tomorrow: today, no court robes. Each rested in their own way, still the same team in different scenery.'},
  {ch:466, n:'The Sea at Dragonvale', t:'On their first true day of rest Jade and Devon had no plans, Sally and Levi found the same wine by accident, Sky went looking for Jenika, and Sera thought about a few days in Altan.'},
  {ch:467, n:'The Healer Who Stayed Behind', t:'While the others rested, Jenika kept working at her healing hall. Sky brought her records of people who believed they were born to be alone, and of those who found a way through by naming it, sharing it and building bonds. The curse had begun with loneliness; the answer might begin with someone willing to keep searching.'},
  {ch:468, n:'Half of Valen', t:'Sky found that Valen traditions describe a pattern of separation, not a wound, which a bond of recognition could interrupt. Sky\'s mother was from Valen and Jenika carries half of it. He may not be the cure, but he may be part of the answer.'},
  {ch:469, n:'A Princess Going Home', t:'Sera returned to Altan for several days, hoping Hugh might say something more; he told her only to enjoy her time at home. After she left he noticed her absence far more than he expected, and that he had still said nothing that mattered.'},
  {ch:470, n:'The Wife Who Brought Her Books', t:'Newly married, Delilah unpacked her books instead of her bridal chests and kept studying military law, logistics, contracts, port agreements and deployment planning while pregnant. Roc promised her the time, resources and peace she needed, and she promised to take breaks.'},
  {ch:471, n:'The Wife Who Refuses to Rest', t:'Roc grew protective as Delilah\'s pregnancy advanced, and Delilah grew annoyed at being treated as incapable of reading documents. She agreed to meals, sensible hours and delegated summaries, but refused to stop studying: pregnancy changed the logistics of her life, not her identity.'},
  {ch:472, n:'Wifely Duties', t:'On a rare quiet day at home Devon teased Jade that she forgot she had a husband. She answered that his complaint was a request, and that her duties for the day were reading, resting, eating well and letting him take care of her. No missions, no court, no world to save: just husband and wife.'},
  {ch:473, n:'Apparently Still No Strings', t:'At a village tavern with no crisis, matchmaker, family argument or investigation, Sally and Levi found themselves drinking together again. Neither wanted a label: a good evening does not need one, and Sally liked this version of their evenings.'},
  {ch:474, n:'A Letter from Altan', t:'Sera wrote from Altan that she was enjoying being home with Rheon and might stay a few more days, and that she still thought of someone who was not there. In Tribute Hugh insisted that her return was only a diplomatic matter, while those around him said they all knew it was more than that.'},
  {ch:476, n:'The Pattern Beneath the Curse', t:'At the Valen research hall Sky and Jenika found that her curse is not a corrosive one but a spiritual separation pattern that keeps threads from stabilising. Valen healing guides such patterns instead of breaking them, and Sky\'s resonance could give hers something steady to learn from.'},
  {ch:477, n:'Not Because You Love Me', t:'Jenika asked whether the cure worked because Sky cared for her. He said it worked because he carries Valen resonance, which can realign and stabilise her scattered pattern, but that caring about her may be why he kept looking. The resonance made healing possible; caring made the answer worth finding.'},
  {ch:478, n:'A Small Disturbance', t:'Fishermen at the coastal village reported moving lights at night: those who followed them lost hours. Jade said not to assume it was one of the Fifteen Evils. Hugh\'s message said the holiday had ended on its own, and the party went out at night to investigate from a safe distance.'},
  {ch:479, n:'The Lanterns Beneath the Water', t:'The party gathered the fishermen\'s accounts, the shoreline routes, Sky\'s reading of the old layered residue, and Sally\'s older records of the same lights thirty and fifty years ago. The phenomenon has a long history on this coast, but the lights are stronger now and more people are disappearing.'},
  {ch:480, n:'What the Sea Remembers', t:'The lights were the memories of sailors who never returned home, left at an ancient half-submerged Dragonvale memorial site. They were not an active curse and not enemies: the party chose to help them find peace with a proper ritual, so their memories could reach the shore and no sailor be forgotten.'}
);

/* ---- Arc XIX, chapter 475 ---- */
LOCATIONS.coastal_village.spots.push(
  {id:'hz475a', kind:'investigate', n:'Routes and Contacts', icon:'🗺️', ch:475, need:2, ambush:[], lo:96, roles:['jade', 'levi', 'sally', 'sky', 'devon'],
   desc:'Sally sketches.',
   clues:['The party spends a peaceful afternoon in the coastal village. With no urgent matters to attend to, everyone takes time to rest, prepare, and enjoy this rare moment of calm together. Sally: "These coastal routes could be useful for future information gathering... Let me note the key locations and who we might be able to ask next time."', 'Sally sketches at a market stall.'], rw:{xp:499100, gold:102120}},
  {id:'hz475b', kind:'investigate', n:'A Little Maintenance', icon:'🏹', ch:475, need:2, ambush:[], lo:96, roles:['jade', 'levi', 'sally', 'sky', 'devon'],
   desc:'Levi\'s bow.',
   clues:['Levi: "A little maintenance now makes a big difference later. The sea air can be harsh on equipment... Better keep everything in good condition."', 'Sky: "There\'s still so much to learn. It\'s a good opportunity to go through these records in peace."'], rw:{xp:499400, gold:102180}, needFlag:'inv_hz475a', lockMsg:'🔒 Finish the previous clue first'},
  {id:'hz475c', kind:'investigate', n:'Without Any Pressure', icon:'🌊', ch:475, need:2, ambush:[], lo:96, roles:['jade', 'levi', 'sally', 'sky', 'devon'],
   desc:'Jade and Devon.',
   clues:['Jade: "The sea breeze feels wonderful today. It\'s nice to simply walk like this without any pressure."', 'Devon: "Yes. Moments like these remind me why we continue our journey. To see places like this... And to have all of you by my side."'], rw:{xp:499700, gold:102240}, needFlag:'inv_hz475b', lockMsg:'🔒 Finish the previous clue first'},
  {id:'hz475d', kind:'investigate', n:'I Will Rest Soon', icon:'🤰', ch:475, need:2, ambush:[], lo:96, roles:['jade', 'levi', 'sally', 'sky', 'devon'],
   desc:'Roc and Delilah.',
   clues:['Meanwhile, Roc: "You\'ve been studying for a while now, Delilah. How about taking a nap? Both you and the baby should get some rest. I worry about you... Promise me you won\'t push yourself too hard."', 'Delilah: "I\'m still fine. There are a few more notes I\'d like to finish. This is actually a good time to organize everything while my mind is clear. But I will rest soon, I promise." For now, there are no battles to fight, no urgent duties calling. Just a quiet afternoon, good company, and the simple joy of being together.'], rw:{xp:500000, gold:102300}, needFlag:'inv_hz475c', lockMsg:'🔒 Finish the previous clue first'},
);
