LORE.push(
  {ch:482, n:'The First Attempt', t:'Sky and Jenika privately attempted treatment: Jenika opened her own power while Sky guided and stabilised the flow. The curse loosened and fragments peeled away, but the core was too deep to remove. Her condition stabilised, and it felt lighter and quieter.'},
  {ch:483, n:'Not Alone', t:'In a second private treatment the curse stirred and whispered that closeness cannot last. Jenika held on and, for the first time, could resist the pull. It was not a cure, but she knew it could be resisted, and that she was not alone.'},
  {ch:484, n:'Two Heartbeats?', t:'During a routine check Jenika sensed that Delilah may be carrying more than one child, though nothing was confirmed. Roc was alarmed and happy at once; Delilah stayed calm and practical: if there were two, they would adjust and prepare.'},
  {ch:485, n:'Double Trouble', t:'A follow-up examination confirmed that Delilah is carrying twins: two distinct, steady rhythms, close but separate. Roc was thrilled and terrified; Delilah stayed calm, saying it was not a crisis but a bigger future, and that she would keep studying within sensible limits.'},
  {ch:486, n:'The Missing Variable', t:'Sky obtained more complete Valen records on soul resonance treatments. They stress constancy, repeated proximity and shared rhythm over raw strength, and mention contact, shared meditation and touch. One phrase, "complete union", appears in several records and Sky could not yet interpret it: the missing variable.'},
  {ch:487, n:'Closer Than Before', t:'In a deeper stage of treatment Jenika learned to hold Sky\'s resonance within her own spirit. When the curse surged she chose to stay connected, and the pull faded: the curse had not ended, but she was learning to resist it, and his resonance was becoming a true anchor.'},
  {ch:488, n:'A Princess Comes Back', t:'Sera returned from Altan refreshed and happy. She learned that Hugh had asked more than once when she was returning, and that he insisted it was purely diplomatic. She did not confront him, and was noticeably happier around him: for now it was enough that he was no longer pretending not to care.'},
  {ch:489, n:'The Things We Return To', t:'After weeks at the coast the whole party gathered again. Jenika was not cured but closer; Delilah and Roc were adjusting to twins; Sally and Levi remained undefined and inseparable; Jade and Devon had had a holiday; and Hugh was getting worse at pretending Sera\'s return was only diplomatic. They went back to their routines and their unfinished missions.'},
  {ch:490, n:'When the Road Calls Again', t:'The holiday ended. Jade opened the letter she had left unopened, Sky arranged to carry the Valen research, Roc and Delilah saw them off, and Sera rejoined the party while Sally stayed available as a recurring travelling ally. This time they had actually had a holiday; now the road called again, and they went with Jade.'},
  {ch:492, n:'I\'m Coming With You', t:'Aster insisted on joining the next journey through the Empire\'s border territories (Westreach, the Riverlands and the northern trade routes), wanting to see the land and its people instead of knowing them only from reports. Jade agreed on condition that he follow her lead and the same rules as everyone else: a working journey, not a leisure trip.'}
);

